    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ENG4_U02_L03_Q01</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.ENG4.R.03</p><p><strong>Passage:</strong> Nadia pressed her palm against the old orchard gate while her brother Tomas unfolded the developer&#39;s letter. The trees behind them were bent and hollow in places, but in spring they still filled the road with white blossoms. &quot;The offer pays every debt,&quot; Tomas said. &quot;It gives us a future.&quot; Nadia looked past him to the rows their grandmother had planted after arriving with two suitcases and no English. &quot;It gives us money,&quot; she answered. &quot;That is not the same thing.&quot; Tomas folded the letter carefully, as if neatness could make the decision merciful. &quot;Grandmother wanted us safe,&quot; he said. Nadia opened the gate and stepped inside. &quot;She also wanted us rooted.&quot; Which statement best describes Tomas&#39;s perspective?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
